					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sinn1sl0ken" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2019868); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2019868&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380249" alt="sinn1sl0ken" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2019868)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sinn1sl0ken" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2019868); return false;" >sinn1sl0ken</a></span> <span class="odate time_1495480037 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 May 2017 19:07</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2829403">
									

<p>I'm really on the fence about this one. As an overall concept, it's interesting, but the concept that it changes the meaning of the language to meet its own ends seems to suggest that most people would have abandoned the language the moment it became an unreliable form of communication; the moment it was clear you could speak a language that gave you no agency, it seems likely you'd give it up unless the changes were extraordinarily subtle. The interview log does not give the indication that it's particularly subtle, so it's a hard sell.</p>
<p>This also seems like an anomaly that could be easily contained by amnesticizing or isolating 3027-1 and securing the dictionary. Interview log 3027-b sort of lampshades this by having the doctor and 3027-1 discuss how easy it would be to eliminate any risk of the language spreading. Likewise, there's no reason to have images of 3027's linguistic maps be unclassified images in the file, so the included images seem to represent the kind of cognitohazard that would be redacted in most containment procedures.</p>
<p>It's not quite a downvote because the idea is fully formed and well written, but it does stretch plausibility pretty far to believe that this language managed to dominate an entire reality and the Foundation's containment procedures seem suspect as described here. No vote for me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
