					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cannedbread" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3099858); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3099858&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380249" alt="CannedBread" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3099858)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cannedbread" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3099858); return false;" >CannedBread</a></span> <span class="odate time_1495565879 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 May 2017 18:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2830388">
									

<p>I had the researcher bring it to our world to study the language in a relatively controlled, low-risk environment. This thing is really powerless if only one person speaks it, and studying anomalies is a big part of the Foundation's MO.</p>
<p>As for the 'do something horrible,' I think this language accomplishing its goal would be horrible enough; for one thing, it would basically control all human thought, and also it would erase entire cultures. (Worth noting that <a href="/scp-2112">SCP-2112</a> is a Keter for approximately that reason.)</p>
<p>And yeah, I'm starting to regret not having the grammar book breach containment&#8212; I described it in detail and everything, it really would have made a good Chekhov's gun! I might revise this at some point to have more action in it.</p>

							</div>

								
